form rather than the creators of games hosted there.","Access type","unavailable","access","section","Platform listing is not game source — Creators may publish source separately, but a game page or downloadable binary alone is not complete project source.","service","demo",[76],{"_57":77,"_25":78,"_79":80},"Browse games on itch.io","https://itch.io/games","note","Independent game catalog with both browser and downloadable games. Availability and license vary by project.","tutorial",[83],{"_57":84,"_25":85,"_79":86},"Create your first itch.io page","https://itch.io/docs/creators/getting-started","Official guide to project information, uploads, classification, publishing, and updates.","Source reviewed","2026-10-20","verified","metadata","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[97,98],"dimensions","2D","3D","Development stages",[102],"stages","Build & release","Topics",[106,107,108,109],"tags","Publishing","Game discovery","Browser games","Desktop games","Further reading",[112,113],{"_57":77,"_25":78},{"_57":84,"_25":85},"Project source",[116],{"_57":114,"_25":117},"https://itch.io/developers","Why it belongs here","itch.io lets creators manage game pages, screenshots, files, development logs, and updates. HTML5 builds can run in the browser; other releases can be provided as downloads with platform labels. A project's page can also contain a demo or work in development, so inspect the actual uploads and instructions. Publishing a playable build does not automatically make its source public.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Community","Category","Game production","category","lead","summary","name","production","community",[145,146],{"_81":140,"_74":141,"_32":142},[106,107,108,109],[139],[137,138],"2d","3d","ship",{"_57":84,"_25":85,"_17":81,"_79":86},{"_57":77,"_25":78,"_17":73,"_79":80},{"_57":143,"_17":69,"_79":144},"Platform listing is not game source","Creators may publish source separately, but a game page or downloadable binary alone is not complete project source